  "caveats": [
    "DECODING: reasoning disabled at the provider key level for every model and every arm, identically, exactly as in L1. The question asked is therefore whether the representation is directly legible without a deliberation subsidy; a large reasoning budget was not tested and was operationally infeasible (it produced provider gateway 502s in L1).",
    "SCALE: development ablation -- 3 tasks, 11 questions, N=3, 33 paired cells per model per arm, 132 pooled per arm. A development signal, not a significance test; strength comes from the consistent direction across four independent families and from the mechanism axes going to exactly zero.",
    "PROVIDER IDENTITY: provider routing identity was verified by the qualified boundary (requested == reported on every attempt, no substitution), but underlying community-hosted weights were not independently attested; model self-identification was inconsistent and is treated as non-authoritative output. This is a limit of provider identity assurance, not a substitution failure.",
    "STRUCTURAL: both Qodec arms are byte-lossless (exact decode roundtrip verified on all three protected encodings). Every difference measured here is model comprehension, not fidelity.",
    "ABSOLUTE BASELINE: RAW correctness is modest (12-22 of 33) because these are small/mid open models with reasoning off. The load-bearing quantities are within-model relative differences."
  ],
