  "finding": "Identifier protection eliminated referential corruption completely and did not restore parity. Across 4 model families, 33 paired cells per model per arm (132 pooled per arm), protecting every observation identity drove fabricated/garbled identifiers from 19 to 0 and leaked legend glyphs from 23 to 0 -- exactly the RAW baseline of zero on both axes -- and recovered most of the correctness gap (FULL_ALIAS 48 -> PROTECTED 64, RAW 70). But no model reached zero paired hard regressions, so non-inferiority fails everywhere, and the residual deficit sits almost entirely in missing_required_witness (RAW 57, PROTECTED 68, FULL_ALIAS 75): the model still reads the compressed grammar less thoroughly than raw JSON even when every identifier is literal. GLM-4.7 is the decisive witness that the residual is NOT about identifiers -- its FULL_ALIAS arm had zero fabrications and zero glyph leaks yet still lost 17 -> 14, and protection moved it only to 15 with hard regressions unchanged at 6.",
